ai-client-empty-diff = There are no changes for AI to summarize.
ai-models-unsupported = This relay does not support listing models. Enter a model name manually.
ai-models-invalid-response = Invalid model list response. Check the URL or enter a model name manually.
ai-summary-generate = Generate with AI
ai-client-key-in-content = The prompt, model, or changes contain the current API key. Remove the key before sending.
ai-summary-generating = Generating with AI…
ai-summary-stop = Stop generating
ai-summary-stopped = Generation stopped. Your commit message has been kept.
ai-summary-clear = Clear
ai-summary-resize-hint = Drag to resize. Double-click to restore automatic height.
ai-summary-save-first = Selected files have unsaved edits. Save them before generating a commit message.
ai-summary-stale = The repository or selected changes have changed. Generate again. Your commit message has been kept.
ai-summary-testing = Testing AI connection…
ai-summary-test-ok = AI connection test succeeded.
ai-summary-preview = AI commit message preview
ai-summary-preview-hint = Full preview opened. Click Replace message above the commit box to use it. Your current message is kept.
ai-summary-replace = Replace message
ai-summary-ready = AI commit message is ready. You can edit it and commit manually.
git-ai-diff-unreadable = Could not read the selected changes. Refresh and try again.
git-ai-diff-too-large = The selected changes exceed the AI input limit. Select fewer files.
git-ai-diff-operation = AI commit messages are unavailable during a merge, rebase, or similar operation.
git-ai-diff-unsupported = Cannot safely read the actual commit content of { $path }. Uncheck it and try again.
git-ai-diff-read-failed = Could not read a selected file: { $error }
ai-client-request-too-large = The selected changes or prompt exceed the AI request limit. Select fewer changes.
ai-client-invalid-url = Invalid AI endpoint. Use an HTTPS base URL or full chat/completions URL; HTTP is allowed for local testing.
ai-client-model-required = Configure an AI model name first.
ai-client-key-required = Configure a valid AI API key first. Keys cannot contain whitespace or line breaks.
ai-client-invalid-response = The AI returned an invalid commit message. Your original message has been kept.
ai-client-incomplete-response = The AI response is incomplete or filtered. Adjust the model or select fewer changes and try again.
ai-client-credential-failed = Cannot access the system credential store. Check your keychain or use the WINC_AI_API_KEY environment variable.
ai-client-cancelled = The AI request was cancelled.
ai-client-curl-unavailable = Cannot run curl. Install or repair your system curl and try again.
ai-client-network-failed = The AI request failed. Check the relay endpoint and network connection.
ai-client-timeout = The AI request timed out. Try again later.
ai-client-response-too-large = The AI response exceeds the size limit. Adjust the model or prompt and try again.
ai-client-redirect-rejected = The relay returned a redirect. To protect your API key, configure the final API endpoint directly.
ai-client-http-failed = The AI API request failed (HTTP { $status }). Check the endpoint, key, and model.
